s://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Part of the worlds design program: [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955). Wave-2 follow-up from the prior-art research (Lane B item 40); parent topic issue: [#5970](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5970). Research source: `workspace/scratch/worlds-capabilities-brief-2026-11-04/prior-art-research.md`.\n\n## Precedent: VRChat, the strong one\n\nVRChat computes an **Avatar Performance Rank** (Excellent → Very Poor) from *measured* metrics — triangles, materials, texture memory, PhysBones, particles, lights, shader complexity. Each user sets a minimum displayed rank; below-threshold avatars are replaced by fallbacks/impostors; **Very Poor is hidden by default**; Quest/mobile has a separate, stricter rank table and only SDK mobile shaders are permitted on Android avatars at all. World/instance settings add another gate layer, and per-user \"Show Avatar\" overrides exist for trusted individuals — the same override shape as our permission and license systems (https://wiki.vrchat.com/index.php?title=Avatar_Performance_Ranking ; https://vrcreators.net/docs/vrchat/quest-compatibility-checklist).\n\n## Scope\n\n#5970 owns per-world enablement of assets/filters; this follow-up designs the **ranking mechanism** that makes gating automatic and legible:\n\n- Measured cost metrics for sprites/filters/shaders (the shader asset format is a sibling follow-up under #5955) and the rank table.\n- Three gate layers: per-world (author policy — e.g. filters off because invisibility cheats), per-viewer (minimum rank), per-person override.\n- **Fallback substitution:** below-threshold content is replaced by its authored fallback (per #5970's fallback chain), never just vanished — except where the world says hidden.\n\nUsers accept automatic visual downgrade when the rule is legible (a rank) and overridable per-person. That is the usability bar.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA ranking design: metrics, rank table, gate layers, substitution rules.\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/6012/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/6012/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}